    "https://careers.umassd.edu/en-us/job/530125/assistant-teaching-professor-director-of-bar-success": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor & Director of Bar Success",
      "description": "Jobs at UMass Dartmouth | Details - Assistant Teaching Professor & Director of Bar Success Skip to main content Support UMassD Directory Check My Status myUMassD University of Massachusetts Dartmouth Search UMass Dartmouth Menu About Admissions Academics Research Outreach Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends Jobs at UMass Dartmouth Toggle navigation from this section Toggle share controls Share on Facebook Share this on X Share on LinkedIn Print this page Email this page Copy URL Link copied to clipboard! University of Massachusetts Dartmouth HOME About // Administration // Human Resources // Jobs at UMass Dartmouth Close Jobs at UMass Dartmouth A great place to work UMass Dartmouth is a vibrant university dedicated to engaged learning and innovative research. Join us in our mission to support student success, foster academic excellence, and promote diverse collaboration. UMassD is a great place to work! Search by keyword Assistant Teaching Professor & Director of Bar Success Apply now Job no: 530125 Work type: Faculty Full Time Categories: Faculty Assistant Teaching Professor and Director of Bar Success Position Announcement The University of Massachusetts School of Law – Dartmouth invites applications for the position of Assistant Teaching Professor and Director of Bar Success. The professor’s responsibilities will include: designing, implementing, and managing the Bar Success Program; teaching bar preparation courses to upper-level students; collaborating with the faculty and administration to develop programming that promotes first-time bar passage; partnering with the Director of Academic Success and the Director of Teaching and Learning Methods to ensure and promote consistent academic assistance from orientation through licensure; in collaboration with the Director of Academic Success, managing MPRE preparation; supervising the Assistant Director for Bar Success; managing the program budget; monitoring bar takers’ progress throughout the year and over the summer; managing relationships with bar review vendors; selecting and overseeing external tutors in the Bar Success Program; developing and implementing a summer bar preparation program; attending out-of-state trainings and conferences to keep current on best practices regarding bar passage, changes to the bar exam and alternative pathways to licensure; working with the Registrar’s office and the administration to track and report on bar passage; and other duties as assigned. The successful candidate will serve as Director of Bar Success and hold the rank of Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor, depending on experience. Assistant Teaching Professors are eligible for promotion to Associate and Full Teaching Professor and may earn continuous appointment. The position will begin July 1, 2027. Applicants must be available to teach in the day and evening divisions as needed. Minimum qualifications: Applicants must have a J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school; strong academic credentials; familiarity with the Uniform Bar Exam, the NextGen Bar Exam, and other jurisdiction-specific requirements for licensure; at least two years of experience in law practice or teaching; and prior bar or academic success experience. Preferred qualifications: Experience with curriculum design, assessment, and data collection. The law school especially welcomes applications from candidates who bring a blend of law practice and teaching experience to their approach to classroom pedagogy and the student experience. We strongly encourage applications from people of color, women, individuals with disabilities, LGBTQ people, veterans, and others whose background, experience, and viewpoints would contribute to a diverse and inclusive environment. The University of Massachusetts School of Law is located on the beautiful south coast of Massachusetts in Dartmouth, MA. It is 60 miles south of Boston and 30 miles east of Providence, RI. We are the state’s only public law school and hold a strong commitment to providing an excellent, affordable legal education. We are also dedicated to improving the quality and reach of justice in Massachusetts and beyond and seek candidates who share that commitment. University of Massachusetts Dartmouth employees and applicants for employment are protected by federal laws, Presidential Executive Orders, and state and local laws designed to protect employees and job applicants from discrimination on the bases of race, religion, color, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, military service, veteran status or other non-merit based factors. The University of Massachusetts reserves the right to conduct background checks on all potential employees. SALARY: Assistant Teaching Rank - $75,000-$88,000 Director of Bar Success annual stipend – 33% of base salary UMass Dartmouth offers exciting benefits such as: 75% Employer-Paid Health Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts Life Insurance Long Term Disability State Pension Retirement Plan Optional Retirement Savings Plans Tuition Credit (Employee, Spouse, & Dependents) Twelve (12) paid holidays And More! Benefits for Faculty Federation To apply, please submit a letter of interest, a current CV, and the contact information for three professional references. The University will consider employment-based visa sponsorship, however, consistent with the Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, UMass Dartmouth will not sponsor H-1B visa petitions that require the mandatory $100,000 payment for any filings submitted after 12:01 a.m. EDT on September 21, 2025. The review of applications will be ongoing until the position is filled. Advertised: 04 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Closes Assistant Teaching Professor & Director of Bar Success The School of Law at the University of Massachusetts Dartmouth is accepting applications for an Assistant Teaching Professor & Director of Bar Success in the Faculty Law School Department. Current opportunities Position Closes Assistant Teaching Professor & Director of Bar Success The School of Law at the University of Massachusetts Dartmouth is accepting applications for an Assistant Teaching Professor & Director of Bar Success in the Faculty Law School Department. Expression of interest Loading... Powered by PageUp The University of Massachusetts Dartmouth welcomes all qualified applicants and complies with all state and federal anti-discrimination laws. Clery Disclosure Notice of Availability In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, the University of Massachusetts Dartmouth publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. This report includes current security policies plus crime and fire statistics for the previous three calendar years. The body of the report also contains contact information for various campus and community resources related to crime prevention and survivor assistance. A digital copy of the report can be accessed on Jeanne Clery & Campus Security Authority. Additional information and resources Refine your search Position Type Faculty Full Time 1 Categories Faculty 1 Applicant Login Login to complete your application and/or apply for more positions. Login Job Alerts We'll send you an e-mail when a position becomes available that matches your search criteria. Subscribe Human Resources Visit Human Resources for more information on benefits, payroll, health insurance, retirement and general information about working at UMass Dartmouth. Visit Last modified: Thu, Nov 13, 2025, 09:15 by Kamryn Kobel Back to top of page Visit us from anywhere, at any time. Take a virtual tour of the UMass Dartmouth campus. Visit us virtually University of Massachusetts Dartmouth 285 Old Westport Road, Dartmouth, MA 02747-2300 Extraordinary is what we do. ® Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram TikTok YouTube Linked in Directions Jobs at UMassD Annual Security Report Privacy Site Map Contact myUMassD Support UMassD Directory Apply Visit Request Info Check Application Status Accessibility Report an accessibility issue Dark Mode Off © 2026 University of Massachusetts Dartmouth + t 4 Close main menu Check My Status myUMassD Support UMassD Directory Search UMass Dartmouth About Accreditation History of UMass Dartmouth Mission and Vision Location Fast Facts Points of Distinction Event Calendar Chancellor's Office Feature Stories News & Press Releases Video Giving Administration UMass System Social Media Flags Staff Directory Contact Accessibility at UMass Dartmouth Help Admissions Apply to UMass Dartmouth Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions UMass Dartmouth Online International Admissions Check your application status Academics Academic Calendar Academic Programs Academic Resource Center Catalogs Centers Claire T. Carney Library Colleges and Schools Courses Faculty Graduate Programs Interdisciplinary Programs International Programs Office Office of Faculty Development Provost Registrar Sigma Xi STEM Student Success UMass Dartmouth Online University Studies Research About Research at UMassD Research Offices Contact Us Openings Outreach Business Engagement Center Campus Sustainability Early College Partnerships Economic Development Government Relations Institutional Partnerships International Partnerships Media Relations Office of Civil Rights Town of Dartmouth University Advancement University Centers Student Life Campus Center Career Center