e of Nursing and Health Sciences Monika Shuler, Adult Nursing Jennifer Viveiros, Adult Nursing Promotion to Senior Lecturer College of Arts & Sciences Caitlin Amaral, English and Communication Randall Hall, Economics Biyong Luo, Mathematic Peter Sandby-Thomas, Political Science September 2021 Faculty promoted or granted tenure effective September 2021 Promotion to Commonwealth Professor School for Marine Science & Technology Mark Altabet, Estuarine & Ocean Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Anna Klobucka, Portuguese Trina Kershaw, Psychology Christopher Larkosh, Portuguese Elizabeth Richardson, Psychology Charlton College of Business Dan Braha, Decision & Information Science Shouhong Wang, Decision & Information Science College of Engineering Walaa Mogawer, Civil & Environmental Engineering Promotion to Professor College of Arts & Sciences Yanlai Chen, Mathematics Michelle Cheyne, Global Languages and Cultures Christopher Eisenhart, English & Communication College of Engineering Robert Fisher, Physics Charlton College of Business Soheil Sibdari, Decision & Information Sciences College of Nursing and Health Sciences Susan Hunter Revell, Adult Nursing Tenure College of Arts & Sciences Marta Del Pozo, Global Languages and Cultures Katherine DeLuca, English & Communications Margarita Huayhua, Sociology & Anthropology Jay Zysk, English & Communication Charlton College of Business Wencheng Joseph Chang, Management & Marketing College of Nursing and Health Sciences Dorothy Dunn, Community Nursing Promotion to Senior Lecturer College of Arts & Sciences Olusegun Olubanwo, Chemistry & Biochemistry Promotion to Librarian Sonia Pacheco September 2020 Faculty promoted or granted tenure effective September 2020 Promotion to Professor College of Arts & Sciences Maureen Eckert, Philosophy Trina Kershaw, Psychology Christopher Larkosh, Portuguese Elizabeth Richardson, Psychology College of Engineering Honggang Wang, Electrical & Computer Engineering Xiaoqin Zhang, Computer & Information Science Charlton College of Business Jia Wu, Accounting & Finance College of Nursing and Health Sciences Mary McCurry, Adult Nursing Tenure College of Arts & Sciences Patrick Cappillino, Chemistry & Biochemistry Jennifer Fugate Shakhnoza Kayumova, Education Eric Larson, Crime and Justice Studies Lucas Mann, English & Communication Joshua Masse, Psychology Maricris Mayes, Chemistry & Biochemistry Nicholas Santavicca, English & Communication Alexis Teagarden, English & Communication Donghui Yan, Mathematics Charlton College of Business Arpita Joarder, Management & Marketing Gang Wang, Decision & Information Sciences John Williams, Management & Marketing College of Engineering Firas Khatib, Computer & Information Science Milana Vasudev, Bioengineering College of Nursing and Health Sciences Caterina Miraglia, Medical Lab Science Law School Margaret Drew Rebecca Flanagan Elizabeth McCuskey College of Visual and Performing Arts Lawrence Jenkens, Art Education, Art History & Media Studies School for Marine Science & Technology Gavin Fay, Fisheries Oceanography Promotion to Senior Lecturer College of Nursing and Health Sciences Kathleen Elliot, Adult Nursing Teresa Reynolds, Adult Nursing Promotion to Librarian Hilary Kraus Promotion to Professional Technician I Carl Leidhold, Chemistry & Biochemistry Paula Wilson, Chemistry & Biochemistry UMass Dartmouth Faculty News Wei-Shun Chang receives $700K National Science Foundation CAREER Award grant for nanoparticle research The NSF CAREER Award will support Chang's research on nanomaterial structure and spin behavior to develop new uses UMass Law professor quoted by Bloomberg Law on Exxon's legal strategy in MA climate litigation Sean Lyness featured in Bloomberg Law coverage of the ongoing legal dispute in the climate change litigation battle of Commonwealth v. Exxon Mobil Corp UMass Law professor publishes essay on equal protection and reparative policy Lisa Lucile Owens introduces the “Historical Racial Nexus” framework as a historically grounded approach to race-conscious policymaking within modern constitutional doctrine News & Press Releases 381 Full-time faculty 260 Tenure/Tenure-track faculty 73.0% Faculty holding terminal degrees 15:1 Student/Faculty ratio Assistant Director Office of Faculty Development Assistant Director for Office of Faculty Development The Office of Faculty Development seeks applications for an Assistant Director focused on AI initiatives in teaching and research to begin Spring, 2026. Job Description Assistant Directors in the Office of Faculty Development create and implement university-wide programming that supports best practices in teaching, learning, and assessment; pedagogical innovation across modalities (i.e. face-to-face, blended, fully online); research, scholarship and creative activity; and professional development opportunities for all faculty. This AD position will have a specialized focus leading and supporting AI initiatives in teaching and research. This role will play a critical part in advancing the integration of artificial intelligence across academic programs and research projects, and the AD is expected to develop programs that will attract faculty from a wide spectrum of disciplines, working closely with faculty, staff, and external partners. The ideal candidate will bring a strong background in AI, a passion for innovation in higher education, and the ability to drive interdisciplinary collaboration. Assistant Directors meet regularly with the OFD Director and Advisory Board to develop new initiatives, increase attendance and retention at OFD events, and evaluate program efficacy. Assistant Directors serve a two-year term. Responsibilities Lead and develop a portfolio focused on integrating AI initiatives in teaching and research; Develop at least 4 programs/workshops per semester specific to AI; Work with OFD staff and CITS Instructional Development team to plan an annual conference on current issues in pedagogy and higher education; Work with OFD Director on program initiatives that support the OFD’s mission and meet changing needs of faculty; Work with OFD Director to develop and update OFD website; Work with OFD Administrative Assistant to promote and publicize events; Hold 2 weekly office hours in the Office of Faculty Development; Other duties as assigned. Compensation Course release for one semester per academic year or comparable stipend. Support for professional development related to OFD work will also be provided, as will workspace in the Office of Faculty Development. Eligibility Candidates must be tenure-track or tenured faculty members, must have demonstrable experience working with and using AI in teaching and/or research, a successful research and publication record, experience teaching in a range of instructional modalities, and a strong record of college and/or university service. Applicants should also have a record of participation in and/or development of OFD programming. Interested applicants should discuss their application with their department chairperson and dean prior to submitting an application. To Apply Please send a letter of interest, a curriculum vitae, and a brief statement of support from your department chair to provost@umassd.edu . The deadline for application is 5 pm on Monday, December 22, 2025. Questions should be directed to Dr. Michael Sheriff, OFD Director, at msheriff@umassd.edu . Additional information and resources Last modified: Fri, Feb 20, 2026, 10:29 by Melissa Kinney Back to top of page Visit us from anywhere, at any time. Take a virtual tour of the UMass Dartmouth campus. Visit us virtually University of Massachusetts Dartmouth 285 Old Westport Road, Dartmouth, MA 02747-2300 Extraordinary is what we do. ® Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram TikTok YouTube Linked in Directions Jobs at UMassD Annual Security Report Privacy Site Map Contact myUMassD Support UMassD Directory Apply Visit Request Info Check Application Status Accessibility Report an