    "https://www.umassd.edu/research/openings/": {
      "title": "Director of the Office of Undergraduate Research",
      "description": "Openings | Research | UMass Dartmouth Skip to main content Support UMassD Directory Check My Status myUMassD University of Massachusetts Dartmouth Search UMass Dartmouth Menu About Research at UMassD Research Offices Contact Us Openings Openings Toggle navigation from this section Toggle share controls Share on Facebook Share this on X Share on LinkedIn Print this page Email this page Copy URL Link copied to clipboard! University of Massachusetts Dartmouth HOME Research // Openings Close In this section About Research at UMassD Research Offices Contact Us Openings Openings Current Openings in the Office of Research and Innovation OUR Director Director of the Office of Undergraduate Research About the Office of Undergraduate Research The OUR supports student engagement in research outside the classroom and creative activities across all fields of study at UMass Dartmouth. The office's mission is to promote and strengthen undergraduate research, facilitate opportunities for students, and help students showcase their work. Ultimately, OUR aims to have at least half of all UMassD students engaged in some form of hands-on research, scholarly work, or creative activity during their undergraduate careers. Led by a research-active faculty member serving as Director, and supported by an Associate Director, the OUR reports to the Chief Research Officer and works closely with the Provost's and Deans' offices to offer grants, information sessions, and guidance. The office hosts the annual UMassD Undergraduate Research Symposium, collaborates with faculty interested in mentoring undergraduate researchers, and supports campus partners with related events. Responsibilities of the OUR Director Strategic Leadership & Campus Partnerships Convene and regularly engage the Undergraduate Faculty Research Council to promote and increase the visibility of undergraduate research. Partner closely with the Senate Research Committee to develop plans that increase student engagement. Collaborate with academic departments and the Honors College to organize and spearhead annual undergraduate research and creative work symposia (including 3-Minute Thesis competitions). Lead the development of programming to raise awareness of research activities and opportunities across all disciplines. Student Programs & Mentorship Manage, refine, and expand academic year and summer research programs, including research and conference travel grants. Facilitate meaningful research experiences and celebrate the achievements of both student researchers and their faculty mentors. Develop targeted initiatives to connect underrepresented undergraduate groups with opportunities to acquire hands-on research experience. Organize workshops and information sessions for early-career students to increase awareness of research and funding opportunities. Bring greater awareness to prestigious student awards (e.g., Goldwater, Marshall, Truman, and Rhodes scholarships) with the goal of increasing application and award rates. Funding & Grant Development Identify and develop internal and external funding sources to diversify and broaden participation in undergraduate inquiry. Seek, apply for, and secure national grants to support the university's undergraduate research and creative activities. Communications & Administration Publish the biannual OUR newsletter highlighting the accomplishments of students and mentors. Produce an annual report detailing OUR activities and accomplishments. Develop and maintain an electronic archive of student projects on the OUR online venues. Manage and expand the OUR social media platforms to increase the visibility of UMassD's undergraduate research efforts. Keep the OUR website current and relevant. Archive all office activities in a shared folder. Compensation & Terms Stipend/Release: $15,000 annual stipend or two-course releases (one per semester). The stipend and course releases may be split. Teaching Load: The Director is expected to carry a minimum teaching load of one lecture course per semester. Appointment: The appointment is for three years (9/1/2026 - 8/31/2029) and will be reviewed annually. Additional information and resources Events Sep 9 Sep 9 12:30PM \"The Monsoon Ocean Isn't One-Dimensional: Fronts, Filaments, and Mixing in the Northern Indian Ocean\" SMAST Seminar - DEOS by: Amit Tandon SMAST East 101-103 Sep 9 Sep 9 3:00PM \"Industrial Salmon Farming in Chilean Patagonia\" SMAST Seminar - DFO - September 9, 2026 by: Alex Bocconcelli SMAST East 101-103 Sep 10 Sep 10 10:00AM EAS Doctoral Proposal Defense by Misbah ul Ain Spatial and Spectral CDS Mapping of Chiral Plasmonic and Nanophotonic Systems SENG 311 Sep 11 Sep 11 1:00PM MS Thesis Defense by Jillian A. Mauk, \"Cranberry Pomace Components as a Source of Anti-Inflammatory Natural Products\" MS Thesis Defense by Jillian A. Mauk Violette 210 Sep 11 Sep 11 3:00PM Physics Master of Science Thesis Defense  by Zachary P. Pereira The Black Mirror Construction for Vaidya Spacetime SENG 306 View Full Calendar Research Development Grant Portal Research Development Grant Portal Last modified: Mon, Apr 13, 2026, 12:29 by Ryan Merrill Back to top of page Visit us from anywhere, at any time. Take a virtual tour of the UMass Dartmouth campus. Visit us virtually University of Massachusetts Dartmouth 285 Old Westport Road, Dartmouth, MA 02747-2300 Extraordinary is what we do. ® Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram TikTok YouTube Linked in Directions Jobs at UMassD Annual Security Report Privacy Site Map Contact myUMassD Support UMassD Directory Apply Visit Request Info Check Application Status Accessibility Report an accessibility issue Dark Mode Off © 2026 University of Massachusetts Dartmouth + t 4 Close main menu Check My Status myUMassD Support UMassD Directory Search UMass Dartmouth About Accreditation History of UMass Dartmouth Mission and Vision Location Fast Facts Points of Distinction Event Calendar Chancellor's Office Feature Stories News &